    "working_thesis": "Hannah Arendt's The Human Condition presents a phenomenological and historical analysis of the vita activa (labor, work, and action) and critiques the traditional philosophical subordination of political action to contemplation, while diagnosing the modern rise of society and the dangers of world alienation and thoughtlessness."
